    "result_text": "Done. `BUILD SUCCESS` and all tests green.\n\nI implemented the `initials` field by following the existing `displayName` computed-field idiom, touching just two files:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it serializes to `$.initials`).\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation to the existing `toOwnerDto` method computing initials as the upper-cased first letters of firstName and lastName, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: no changes to the large `Owner`/`Person` entity classes, no new pipeline steps, and the only edited method gains a single declarative annotation line rather than any new branching logic. `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"` as required.",
